{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"O95864","secondaryAccessions":["A8K2M6","B7Z634","Q6MZQ7","Q96H07","Q96SV8","Q9H3G3","Q9Y3X4"],"uniProtkbId":"FADS2_HUMAN","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"2007-10-02","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-09-02","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"1999-05-01","entryVersion":188,"sequenceVersion":1},"annotationScore":5.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Homo sapiens","commonName":"Human","taxonId":9606,"lineage":["Eukaryota","Metazoa","Chordata","Craniata","Vertebrata","Euteleostomi","Mammalia","Eutheria","Euarchontoglires","Primates","Haplorrhini","Catarrhini","Hominidae","Homo"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"12713571"}],"value":"Acyl-CoA 6-desaturase"},"ecNumbers":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12713571"}],"value":"1.14.19.3"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"value":"Delta(6) fatty acid desaturase"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q9Z0R9"}],"value":"D6D"},{"value":"Delta(6) desaturase"},{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"12713571"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"9867867"}],"value":"Delta-6 desaturase"}]},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"10860662"}],"value":"Fatty acid desaturase 2"}}]},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"HGNC","id":"HGNC:3575"}],"value":"FADS2"}}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"B8R1K0"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q9Z122"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12713571"}],"value":"Involved in the biosynthesis of highly unsaturated fatty acids (HUFA) from the essential polyunsaturated fatty acids (PUFA) linoleic acid (LA) (18:2n-6) and alpha-linolenic acid (ALA) (18:3n-3) precursors, acting as a fatty acyl-coenzyme A (CoA) desaturase that introduces a cis double bond at carbon 6 of the fatty acyl chain. Catalyzes the first and rate limiting step in this pathway which is the desaturation of LA (18:2n-6) and ALA (18:3n-3) into gamma-linoleate (GLA) (18:3n-6) and stearidonate (18:4n-3), respectively (PubMed:12713571). Subsequently, in the biosynthetic pathway of HUFA n-3 series, it desaturates tetracosapentaenoate (24:5n-3) to tetracosahexaenoate (24:6n-3), which is then converted to docosahexaenoate (DHA)(22:6n-3), an important lipid for nervous system function (By similarity). Desaturates hexadecanate (palmitate) to produce 6Z-hexadecenoate (sapienate), a fatty acid unique to humans and major component of human sebum, that has been implicated in the development of acne and may have potent antibacterial activity (PubMed:12713571). It can also desaturate (11E)-octadecenoate (trans-vaccenoate, the predominant trans fatty acid in human milk) at carbon 6 generating (6Z,11E)-octadecadienoate (By similarity). In addition to Delta-6 activity, this enzyme exhibits Delta-8 activity with slight biases toward n-3 fatty acyl-CoA substrates (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"(9Z,12Z)-octadecadienoyl-CoA + 2 Fe(II)-[cytochrome b5] + O2 + 2 H(+) = (6Z,9Z,12Z)-octadecatrienoyl-CoA + 2 Fe(III)-[cytochrome b5] + 2 H2O","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:47140"},{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA-COMP:10438"},{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA-COMP:10439"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15377"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15378"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15379"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:29033"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:29034"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:57363"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:57383"}],"ecNumber":"1.14.19.3","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12713571"}]},"physiologicalReactions":[{"directionType":"left-to-right","reactionCrossReference":{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:47141"},"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12713571"}]}]},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"(9Z,12Z,15Z)-octadecatrienoyl-CoA + 2 Fe(II)-[cytochrome b5] + O2 + 2 H(+) = (6Z,9Z,12Z,15Z)-octadecatetraenoyl-CoA + 2 Fe(III)-[cytochrome b5] + 2 H2O","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:47144"},{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA-COMP:10438"},{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA-COMP:10439"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15377"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15378"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15379"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:29033"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:29034"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:71489"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:74034"}],"ecNumber":"1.14.19.3","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q9Z0R9"}]},"physiologicalReactions":[{"directionType":"left-to-right","reactionCrossReference":{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:47145"},"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q9Z0R9"}]}]},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"hexadecanoyl-CoA + 2 Fe(II)-[cytochrome b5] + O2 + 2 H(+) = (6Z)-hexadecenoyl-CoA + 2 Fe(III)-[cytochrome b5] + 2 H2O","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:37023"},{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA-COMP:10438"},{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA-COMP:10439"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15377"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15378"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15379"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:29033"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:29034"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:57379"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:74339"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12713571"}]},"physiologicalReactions":[{"directionType":"left-to-right","reactionCrossReference":{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:37024"},"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO: